# Environment overrides for the gdhcp systemd service, sourced via
# EnvironmentFile= in gdhcp.service. Installed at /etc/gdhcp/gdhcp.env by
# scripts/install.sh (mode 600, owned by gdhcp:gdhcp — this file often holds
# the DB password).
#
# Anything set in /etc/gdhcp/config.yaml can be overridden here instead, as
# GDHCP_<SECTION>_<FIELD> (see server/internal/config/loader.go). Uncomment
# and edit what you need; leave the rest to config.yaml.

# GDHCP_DATABASE_DSN=postgres://gdhcp:changeme@localhost:5432/gdhcp?sslmode=disable
# GDHCP_LOGGING_LEVEL=info
# GDHCP_SERVER_JWT_SECRET=
# GDHCP_HA_ENABLED=false
